Whimsalot, [[Whimsun]]'s CORE/Hard Mode counterpart in Undertale, was for the longest time also the upgraded version of Whimsun in Undercards, with higher stats and a simmilar ability. Only instead of gaining ATK, it gains both ATK and HP for each ally monster in play (so up to +3/+3). Originally, it costed 7G for a 4/4, thus at most effective use, it would be a 7/7/7.

'''Alpha 2.1''' dropped its cost to 6G due to the fact that [[Final Froggit]] (at that time) also costed 7G, but had 6/6 by default, for which Whimsalot needed 2 ally monsters. '''Beta 5.3''' gave it +1 HP, '''Beta 15.0''' +1 cost (bringing it back to 7G) and '''Beta 17.0''' +1 ATK, leaving it with 5/5, so 8/8 at most after its Magic.

It stayed like this until '''Beta 53.1''', where alongside another +1 HP, its Magic was changed. Now, it gives +1/+1 to a random monster in your hand. But still for each other ally monster, this effect is repeated. This means it does it 1-4 times and it can target any monster in your hand each time.

